Sleeping in spring, I did not notice the dawn;
everywhere I hear the birds singing.
In the night came the sound of wind and rain;
who knows how many flowers have fallen?

In spring I sleep and do not notice the dawn;
everywhere I hear the birds singing.
In the night there was the sound of wind and rain;
who knows how many flowers have fallen.

